1. DDL (Data Definition Language)
Purpose: Defines structure of the database and collections.

SQL Examples:
CREATE, ALTER, DROP, TRUNCATE

MongoDB Equivalents:
SQL DDL	MongoDB Equivalent	Use Case
CREATE TABLE	db.createCollection()	Create a new collection
DROP TABLE	db.collection.drop()	Delete a collection
ALTER TABLE	Not directly supported, but use schema validation or custom logic	
TRUNCATE	db.collection.deleteMany({})	Delete all documents without deleting collection


EX:
// Create a collection
db.createCollection("students")

// Drop a collection
db.students.drop()

// Truncate-like behavior
db.students.deleteMany({})


2. DML (Data Manipulation Language)
Purpose: Used to manipulate data inside collections.

SQL Examples:
INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE

MongoDB Equivalents:
SQL DML	MongoDB Command	Use Case
INSERT	insertOne(), insertMany()	Add new documents
UPDATE	updateOne(), updateMany(), replaceOne()	Update document(s)
DELETE	deleteOne(), deleteMany()	Remove document(s)


EX:

// Insert
db.students.insertOne({ name: "Sachin", age: 24 })

// Update
db.students.updateOne(
  { name: "Sachin" },
  { $set: { age: 25 } }
)

// Delete
db.students.deleteOne({ name: "Sachin" })



3. DQL (Data Query Language)
Purpose: Fetch data from collections.

SQL Example:
SELECT

MongoDB Equivalent:
find(), findOne(), with filters, projection, and operators

Use Case:
Fetch documents with various criteria.

MongoDB Examples:

EX:

// Fetch all documents
db.students.find()

// Fetch with condition
db.students.find({ age: { $gt: 20 } })

// Fetch with projection
db.students.find({ age: { $gt: 20 } }, { name: 1, _id: 0 })




4. TCL (Transaction Control Language)
Purpose: Manage transactions in databases (commit, rollback, etc.)

SQL Example:
BEGIN, COMMIT, ROLLBACK

MongoDB Equivalent (Transactions supported in replica sets or sharded clusters):
startSession(), startTransaction(), commitTransaction(), abortTransaction()

MongoDB Example:

EX:

const session = db.getMongo().startSession()
session.startTransaction()

try {
  session.getDatabase("test").students.insertOne(
    { name: "Ravi" }, { session }
  )
  session.getDatabase("test").marks.insertOne(
    { student: "Ravi", score: 90 }, { session }
  )
  session.commitTransaction()
} catch (e) {
  session.abortTransaction()
}
session.endSession()


5. DCL (Data Control Language)
Purpose: Manage permissions and access control.

SQL Example:
GRANT, REVOKE

MongoDB Equivalent:
createUser(), grantRolesToUser(), revokeRolesFromUser()

MongoDB Examples:



EX:

// Create user with read access
db.createUser({
  user: "readUser",
  pwd: "1234",
  roles: [{ role: "read", db: "test" }]
})

// Grant additional role
db.grantRolesToUser("readUser", [{ role: "readWrite", db: "test" }])











